Falsifies `system_tests::user::page_table_region_tests::a_destroyed_region_takes_no_live_spaces_page_tables_with_it`.

Architecture: aarch64, riscv64, x86_64

The defect is the tree as it stood until 2026-10-05 (UTC), as near as the fixed tree can say it:
`revoke_region` finds every page-table record in the destroyed range, tombstones it, and cuts
nothing. The tables
`PageFrame::MAP` and `MemoryRegion::MAP` built out of the region go back to the allocator while the
space still links them. Before the fix nothing recorded them at all; the records the patch leaves
behind are inert, so the space's walk is exactly the old one.

It was recorded in `revoke::revoke_region`'s `BUGS` by the map-revocation-window lane (milestone
762, provisional), reasoned from the code and not driven.

Expected to fail: `assert!(load(&REPORT.tables_from_r2) > 0, "MemoryRegion: a map beside VA after
R's DESTROY built no tables from R2, so it wrote its leaf into a table R had given back ...")`, on
the first round. Confirmed red on aarch64 on 2026-10-05 (UTC) against the fixed tree, at
`page_table_region_tests.rs:236`, the assertion predicted. Before the fix existed, the same test
went red on aarch64 at the same assertion with the `MemoryRegion` round first, and at the
`mapped_after` assertion with the `PageFrame` round first.

**The assertions above the headline stay green under this patch**: the first map spent tables
from R, R's `DESTROY` succeeded and its name no longer resolves, and (for this round, whose leaf is
R's own) the leaf pass still unmapped VA and tombstoned its record.

The patch leaves `cut_user_table` and `forget_mappings_within` unused, so the build warns twice;
it does not fail. Nothing here is architecture-specific, so one patch serves every leg.

**Re-cut 2026-10-20 (UTC) by lane 2451 (cpu-matrix shard budget)**, when `revoke_region` began
taking every leaf in one scan and lost `Victim`. The difference from the fixed tree is unchanged:
the table is tombstoned and not cut. Replayed red on aarch64 the same day, at
`page_table_region_tests.rs:236`, the headline.

diff --git a/kernel/src/revoke.rs b/kernel/src/revoke.rs
--- a/kernel/src/revoke.rs
+++ b/kernel/src/revoke.rs
@@ -1003,11 +1003,7 @@ pub fn revoke_region(base: u64, size: u64) {
             break;
         };
         // Cut under the registry, so no `MAP` is halfway down this walk.
-        if let Some((cut, span)) = mmu::cut_user_table(root, va, table, asid)
-            && let Some(space) = spaces.live_mut().find(|s| s.root == root)
-        {
-            space.forget_mappings_within(cut, span);
-        }
+        let _ = (root, asid, va, table);
     }
 }
 
